WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.500
Each one of the rooms the characters encounter
in Escape Room has an intended solution.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.890
But if Breath of the Wild has taught me anything,
it’s that there are often more than one

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:12.170
possible solution for any given puzzle, and
I don’t think they always found the intended

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:13.170
path.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.480
Stick around to the end of the video if you
want to hear the real solutions for these

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.380
rooms.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:21.480
[INTRO]

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:24.740
Welcome back to Things You Missed and Happy
New Year 2019.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:29.340
I’ve got an exciting week packed with content
for you this week and to kick it all off,

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.550
we’re going to be covering some of the hidden
details and their meanings in the first horror

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.679
movie of the year: Escape Room.

00:00:34.679 --> 00:00:36.640
Let’s start with the beginning of the movie.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.539
The opening shot pulls out from a chess board.

00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:41.540
You’re probably thinking that this is a
microcosm of the entire movie being a chess

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.250
match against the creators of the game, and
the participants are just trying to become

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.729
the last piece standing.

00:00:45.729 --> 00:00:48.420
There’s actually a little bit more to it
than that.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.260
When Zoey heads back to her dorm after class,
there’s a poster advertising a chess group

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.760
meeting at the college.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.989
That might be where she gets some of her deductive
reasoning skills, because I spotted a chess

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.379
piece in her room.

00:00:58.379 --> 00:01:02.149
But it wasn’t just any chess piece, it was
a King, and if you’ve ever played Chess

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:06.600
you know that the King is the one piece that
must remain standing in order for the game

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.750
to continue.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:11.630
So when Zoey faked her death in the hospital
themed room, I knew he hadn’t heard the

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:12.630
last of her.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:16.070
But that’s not the only clue left in the
opening scene, the flash-forward of Ben’s

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.070
final test.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:20.509
There is also some Latin text printed on the
top of the wall near the ceiling that says

00:01:20.509 --> 00:01:25.260
Acta Est Fabula, which roughly translates
to “The Play Is Over” or “The Performance

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.090
Is Over”, a clue that the entire game was
created for entertainment, which is explained

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:30.770
once Ben reaches the final room.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:35.060
That’s not the only clue towards the game
being an entertainment trail for the super-rich.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:37.719
We are first introduced to Zoey at her college
physics lecture.

00:01:37.719 --> 00:01:41.690
Her professor brings up the phrase “A watched
pot never boils”, and explains how that

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:45.950
may actually be true under the Quantum Zeno
effect in which observation stops movement

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:46.950
in atoms.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:51.140
Zoey’s plan for getting out kind of mirrors
that effect, she smashes every camera in the

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:54.689
room so she’s no longer being observed,
then passes out and waits for the cleanup

00:01:54.689 --> 00:02:01.020
crew to come around so she can take them out
and escape.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.400
After that lecture she has a little chat with
her professor, who tells her that reducing

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.100
variables won’t change the outcome.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:10.141
At the time it’s more of a reference to
her life choices of being an introvert, but

00:02:10.141 --> 00:02:14.330
you could also apply it to the game and say
she’s doomed to eventually lose no matter

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:15.330
what.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:17.250
The name of the company who runs the Escape
Room is Minos.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.770
The logo of this company is explained in the
movie, but the name is not.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:22.530
It goes back to ancient Greek mythology.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:27.250
Minos of the first King of Crete who commanded
that seven young boys and seven young girls

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:31.650
be sent into the Labyrinth, a giant maze structure
that houses a minotaur, with the intention

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.780
that they be eaten by the Minotaur.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:37.720
In other words, the company being named Minos
should have been a huge red flag that the

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.950
seven contestants were not meant to survive.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.610
Seven seems to be a recurring number throughout
the movie as well.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:46.310
In addition to the seven contestants when
you add in the guy introduced into the game

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:50.250
at the winners room, there are 7 rooms and
the clue in the second room is a 7 letter

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.250
word.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:54.340
Seven, of course is considered a lucky number,
and the winner of each game is considered

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.540
lucky to be alive.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.310
When Zoey and Ben meet up again after getting
out alive, they get lunch together on St.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.990
Patrick’s day, which is often considered
to be a lucky day.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:04.230
But let’s go back to when the contestants
all meet.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:07.660
Amanda, the redhead girl, reads a newspaper
headline about 5 people being found burned

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.660
alive.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:12.390
I would theorize this is from another iteration
of the game, or a beta testing of the game.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.590
The waiting room turns out to be the first
trial room, the giant oven.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:18.590
Anyone who’s played Ocarina of Time should
have figured out how those weight sensitive

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:22.400
pedestals work, but it didn’t click for
them until it was almost too late.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.070
The obvious intended solution was to fill
up the cups with water and place them on the

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:29.340
switches, however, they didn’t have enough
water because Amanda drank some of it, so

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.860
they ended up using some liquid that Ben had
in a flask.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:36.110
They also could have had someone pee in the
last cup, or place literally any heavy object

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:40.120
in the room on top of the cup, but they were
lucky enough to have the flask on hand.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:44.590
So they moved onto the inside of the cabin,
where they needed a 7-letter word to advance.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.330
If you don’t remember the word was “Rudolf”.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.420
There were three clues in in the cabin and
Ben was able to figure it out having only

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:53.140
found two, the text that said YOU’LL GO
DOWN IN HISTORY, which to be honest should

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.440
have been enough on its own.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.500
The other clue they saw was the reindeer mantles.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.040
Again, probably should have been enough on
their own.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:02.570
But they didn’t seem to notice that the
camera in this room is the only one in the

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:06.010
game with a blinking red recording light,
which could have also tipped them off as a

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.480
clue pointing to Rudolph’s shining red nose.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.790
After solving that puzzle, they move onto
the ice level.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:14.310
It start with them finding the jacket, Zoey
gets to wear it for a bit, and she discovers

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:17.060
the compass with the text, True North is a
lie.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.260
This is actually the same compass seen hanging
from her mother’s pocket when she later

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.980
has the flashback to the plane crash that
killed her family AND the brand of the compass

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:27.710
is Stanley, London and London happens to be
the location she buys the plane tickets to

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:30.500
in order to try to infiltrate Minos at the
end of the movie.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.040
Meanwhile, Mike gets distracted by the Husky
dog, which matches the description of his

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.350
old dog that he told everyone about when they
are all in the waiting room.

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.901
This leads him to find the fishing rod in
the tree.

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:43.100
The compass leads to the magnet and the magnet
goes on the bottom of the fishing rod to help

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.430
them find the ice box with the key.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:48.650
This is where the intended solution is a little
bit unclear, and I don’t really buy that

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:51.090
they are supposed to use the warmth of their
hands to melt the ice.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.410
I do have a theory though.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:55.170
There’s one object that is never used, the
thermometer.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:58.130
Maybe they are supposed to break open the
thermometer and spill out the mercury on the

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.130
ice block.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:02.690
I looked it up, and I guess Mercury is not
flammable, but in the presence of water it

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:03.690
can become explosive.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:07.380
This is assuming that they don’t lose the
lighter, which they do when Danny falls through

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:08.380
the ice.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.570
If you’re an expert on chemistry, let me
know if that would actually work, because

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:12.760
honestly I have no idea.

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:16.440
They also could have potentially started a
fire using branches from tree, so there may

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.380
have been more than one solution there.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.160
Next room is the upside down 8-Ball Room,
where the song ‘Downtown’ plays over and

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:23.380
over on repeat.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:26.720
Everything they need to know to solve this
puzzle is in the lyrics if they had only stopped

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.720
to listen.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:32.040
“Just listen to the music of the the traffic
in the city.”

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.500
It’s literally telling them, stop and listen
to the music first.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:39.560
“Linger on the sidewalk where the neon signs
are pretty.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:42.400
How can you lose.”

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.820
In this case, the “sidewalk” is the area
on the sides of the room, where the floor

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:49.660
isn’t falling away and the “neon signs”
are the color coded puzzle which corresponds

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.610
to the numbers on the balls of the pool table.

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:58.010
It’s telling them if they study these signs,
they won’t lose.

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:01.860
“Downtown, things will be great when you’re
downtown.”

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:04.919
This line is a bit trickier, but basically
it’s telling them to go down, but since

00:06:04.919 --> 00:06:09.040
the room is upside-down they really need to
go up, and that’s where Amanda finds the

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:10.040
safe.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:17.180
“When you’ve got worries all the noise
and the hurry seems to help I know.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.180
Downtown.”

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:20.860
This just lets them know they have limited
time to solve this room.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:28.150
“Don’t hang around and let your problems
surround you there are movie shows.

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:29.150
Downtown.”

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:32.690
Amanda ends up hanging from the telephone
wire, and the problems that surround her are

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:34.220
the bottomless pits on each side of her.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:35.870
I mean, not bottomless, but you know what
I mean.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:39.120
She sits there and “hangs around” and
ends up paying the price for it.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.520
“You may find somebody kind to help and
understand you.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:50.139
Someone who is just like you and needs a gentle
hand to guide them along.”

00:06:50.139 --> 00:06:53.770
The other contestants literally offer Amanda
a helping hand when she’s hanging there,

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:54.790
but she doesn’t take it.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:58.540
This movie is absolutely filled with other
possible clues, so if you caught anything

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:02.400
I didn’t notice in my video -- go ahead
and let me know in the comments.

